","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/e57_xX26SXt8jCtMY_YuYNd_m7jzybgRhdW5ezGybck/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI1MjQz/MDUtMTQzMDk0NzU1/Ni00MjYzLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"A group of producers strictly connected to [l=Early Sounds Recordings] .\r\nMainly formed by its founders [a=Leskin], [url=http://www.discogs.com/artist/754998-Massimo-Di-Lena]Massimo Di Lena[/url] and [url=http://www.discogs.com/artist/1069519]Rio Padice[/url] it can also host some producers closely related to the label .","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:2524305","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":754998,"name":"Massimo Di Lena"},{"active":true,"id":905979,"name":"Dario di Pace"},{"active":true,"id":3360805,"name":"Pellegrino S. Snichelotto"}],"namevariations":["Early Sounds Collective","The Early Sound Collective"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/2524305-The-Early-Sounds-Collective","type":"artist","urls":["https://soundcloud.com/earlysoundsrecordings","https://www.facebook.com/EarlySoundsRec"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/2580655/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"2580655","image":"https://i.discogs.com/V-HIJlqlxLo2nXI7UgzK2GmDDLv37RkA9i85l0ZKLO0/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:337/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI1ODA2/NTUtMTY5MDI3NjE3/NC01MTY2LmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/pYsh_4OxpOGmqgxoyvchZtPxqx06gr0d_7blI_zQTds/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI1ODA2/NTUtMTY5MDI3NjE3/NC01MTY2LmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"Jazz singer","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:2580655","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":[{"active":true,"id":7676319,"name":"Ajoyo"}],"members":null,"namevariations":["Charles","S. E. Charles","SEC","サラ・エリザベス・チャールズ"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/2580655-Sarah-Elizabeth-Charles","type":"artist","urls":["http://www.sarahelizabethcharles.com/","https://sarah-elizabeth-charles.bandcamp.com/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/286117/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"286117","image":"https://i.discogs.com/RSgecRTWAMTY5GrjtLF0-FrnajgHESaIAS_4iVcO_y8/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI4NjEx/Ny0xNzM1MjExNDM5/LTM4MTkuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/s4ScVoIqR6ca7AsSZkZux_Alc0sHM0w4zz-tbXzUxHY/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI4NjEx/Ny0xNzM1MjExNDM5/LTM4MTkuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"Nigerian singing duo consisting of identical twins [a2813421] (died 9 November 2019) and [a2813420], who combined the genres of Afrobeat, funk, reggae, disco and Memphis soul. They were active from the mid-1960s to the 1980s. In 1988 the sisters went on tour to the USA and stayed there.\r\n\r\nTwins Taiwo and Kehinde were born in Jos, in northern Nigeria, on October 22, 1948. In Yoruba, ”Taiwo” means \"the first twin to taste the world”, and ”Kehinde” \"the second-born of the twins”, “the chaperone” or “the one who comes after Taiwo”. Though Taiwo is the firstborn, it is believed that Kehinde is the elder twin, sending Taiwo into the world first to determine if it is time to be born. The names are given to both boys and girls.\r\n\r\nOne of the most popular acts in the Nigerian music scene of the 1970s, The Lijadu Sisters produced a handful of albums showcasing their tight harmonies and inventive incorporation of synthesizers and modern pop forms into funky Afro-beat grooves. Beginning as backing vocalists for studio sessions, the sisters eventually released a single in 1968 under their own name titled Iya Mi Jowo. In 1971, still working as session singers, the sisters met Cream/Africa 70 drummer Ginger Baker, and performed with Baker's band Salt at the 1972 Munich Olympic Games.\r\n\r\nWith the assistance of multi-instrumentalist and producer Biddy Wright, the Lijadu Sisters would make four albums for Decca's Afrodisia imprint: 1976's Danger, 1977's Mother Africa, 1978's Sunshine, and 1979's Horizon Unlimited. These vibrant collisions of pop, reggae, and Afro-beat influences defined the sisters' unique hybrid sound and rocketed them to immense popularity in Nigeria, as well as gaining them the attention of a broader audience internationally.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:286117","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":2813420,"name":"Taiwo Lijadu"},{"active":true,"id":2813421,"name":"Kehinde Lijadu"}],"namevariations":["Lijadu","The Lijadu Sisters"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/286117-Lijadu-Sisters","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.thelijadusisters.com/","https://thelijadusisters.bandcamp.com/","https://www.facebook.com/TheLijaduSisters","https://www.instagram.com/TheLijaduSisters","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lijadu_Sisters","https://republic.com.ng/gender/who-were-the-lijadu-sisters/","https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-features/lijadu-sisters-profile-afropop-legacy-1235035517/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/29979/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"29979","image":"https://i.discogs.com/0065IYugxa3qSFlfZ4DE_LMJ17EQuhISaMz4_q7gl04/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:587/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI5OTc5/LTE3Mjc4MDUyNDgt/ODU4My5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/an_DMJt-4SannpstSBZTywUTs_28gSMfEyk9TEvxw3k/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTI5OTc5/LTE3Mjc4MDUyNDgt/ODU4My5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"American jazz saxophonist and composer\r\nBorn: 25th August 1933 Newark, New Jersey, USA\r\nDied: 2nd March 2023 Los Angeles, California, USA\r\nMember of three seminal jazz groups of the 20th century: the Jazz Messengers led by [a=Art Blakey], [a=The Miles Davis Quintet] & [a=Weather Report]. He was a long-standing collaborator with [a=Joni Mitchell] and won 11 Grammy awards as well a lifetime achievement Grammy.\r\nBrother of trumpeter [a=Alan Shorter]","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:art